<title>USA: Fed seen adding reserves via customer RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed seen adding reserves via customer RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve is expected to add temporary reserves to the banking system on Monday through customer repurchase agreements, market analysts said.</p>
<p>Some analysts also cited the possibility of a three-day system repo, depending on the firmness in funds as the morning unfolds.</p>
<p>At 1055 EDT/1455 GMT, the federal funds rate was trading at 5-3/8 percent, above the Fed's 5-1/4 percent target.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
